{"obsah":"<p><strong>When we're not training, we're performing!</strong></p>\n\n<p>For the last few years Martin Šimůnek has gone to the running races by the artificial lake Milada – Milada Run. An interesting setting, but terrain full of clods probably wouldn't allow any performance other than Trial. This time Martin invited Vlasta Kabeláč Čiháček so he wouldn't have to sweat alone in the heat before the storm, but in the end, despite the rising temperature, it was a really pleasant ride, stretched out with competitions for spectators and jumps over volunteers on the stage. Martin's obstacle setup in green fitted the local environment quite well and is an interesting Trial challenge in itself, and it's a joy to watch how easily Martin handles it, which the spectators appreciated too.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>By coincidence a few visitors from our leisure park in Tehov also came and immediately said hi to the guys. Between exhibitions they got out their full-suspension bikes and rode part of the way around the lake, and of course a swim at the end was a must. </p>\n\n<p>Despite the current situation the turnout was very decent, and we thank the organisers for the invitation – they did an honest piece of work.</p>\n\n<p><br></p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2020%2F08%2FMilada-Run17.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"173765\" data-full-url=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2020%2F08%2FMilada-Run17.webp?alt=media\" data-link=\"https://bikeskills.cz/?attachment_id=173765\" class=\"wp-image-173765\"/></figure></li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2020%2F08%2FMilada-Run1